.SH NAME
anpu-plugin-run - Run a plugin file or registered plugin against a target


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu plugin run [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Execute exactly one plugin source against an authorized target:
either --plugin  (declarative checks) or --name 
(a compiled-in Go plugin, see \fBanpu plugin list\fR). Prints findings
as text, or JSON with --json for scripting. Exits 0 on a completed run
(even with findings); --fail-on is intentionally left to \fBanpu scan\fR\&.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--format\fP="text"
	output format: text or json

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for run

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	registered Go plugin to execute

.PP
\fB--plugin\fP=""
	YAML plugin file to execute


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBanpu-plugin(1)\fP


